      "body": "This patch treats the symptom (EBADF on a closed socket) rather than the root cause. When TCPServer.stop() closes the listening socket, the IOLoop handler for that socket is still registered. The more robust fix is to have add_accept_handler return a callable that removes the handler (via io_loop.remove_handler), and have TCPServer.stop() call it before/when closing the socket, so the accept callback is never invoked on a closed fd. Catching EBADF still leaves the handler registered on a closed/reused fd, which can cause spurious wakeups or (worse) firing on an unrelated fd if the descriptor number is reused. Consider a stop-flag or handler removal approach instead."
