      "title": "Map section decryption should follow HLS spec, not be unconditionally skipped",
      "body": "The change unconditionally skips decryption for all map sections. But per the HLS spec (RFC 8216), an EXT-X-MAP is subject to the EXT-X-KEY that precedes it in playlist order. In this particular playlist the EXT-X-MAP appears *before* the EXT-X-KEY, so the init section is indeed plaintext — but in playlists where EXT-X-KEY precedes EXT-X-MAP, the init section IS encrypted and must be decrypted. Unconditionally disabling map decryption will break those (valid, common) cases.\n\nThe correct fix is at parse time: associate the map with the key that applies to it based on ordering (i.e. the map's key should be None/NONE when no key precedes it, and the applicable key when one does). Then `_write` can keep decrypting based on `segment.key` as before. Please fix the parser to assign the correct key to the map instead of blanket-skipping decryption in the writer."
